{"agent_id":"s005-wave","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-20T22:50:39.097528222Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ba37e7f4-6064-4b09-9f2e-33fb320d2dcf","comment_uuid":"61773e12-6e41-4880-b464-4ddd02bbe9b1","author":"s005-wave","content":"S-005 architecture decision: replace config::Environment underscore rewriting and ad-hoc API-key repair with one finite typed registry. Canonical OPENCLAUDIA names use __ between typed nesting levels and _ inside field/provider segments; exact legacy single-underscore names warn as deprecated, ecosystem provider-key names remain compatibility aliases, and multiple aliases for one field are rejected as ambiguous. Each descriptor carries parser, secrecy, source precedence, deprecation, and security relevance. Values are bounded, parsed, and installed as final builder overrides after project/home files and before explicit CLI mutation so a valid higher-precedence environment value can replace malformed lower-precedence file state. OPENCLAUDIA names owned by other subsystems are explicitly allowlisted; all other prefixed names fail closed. ACP max_iterations adopts the same canonical/legacy rule without expanding into the broader W14 loader-unification work.","created_at":"2026-08-20T22:50:39.070535515Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:GnnQNPlvNEZp35JadXiNDA+I/8ohf5UCKkSJrMb/gew","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgSjog0F9LUCbKsv62g2BnSf4fH0D7kCW68xbgp+h6bYUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAI1jmqU4Oqw7ekZGi/UKdX3gVFF1LrrICpCqFKU5pK7m3HVXVh4CG8UAxZBsxkxJRqTVfqJyslhXmx9MWvwHuAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:GnnQNPlvNEZp35JadXiNDA+I/8ohf5UCKkSJrMb/gew","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgSjog0F9LUCbKsv62g2BnSf4fH0D7kCW68xbgp+h6bYUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQINVqb9+f2Jne7YtXE9Sj3ugDbOiXWfewTKqE0jtH0VTqTv65MGEnfAe0ZRJ/MrfB+68LIwFCc4BXrC02VQUMA8="}
{"agent_id":"s005-wave","agent_seq":3,"timestamp":"2026-08-20T23:02:06.940282464Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ba37e7f4-6064-4b09-9f2e-33fb320d2dcf","comment_uuid":"0fe4b106-150c-431b-a921-23404785cab4","author":"s005-wave","content":"S-005 decision amendment: do not use ConfigBuilder::set_override for typed environment tables. config 0.15 deep-merges table overrides, which would retain lower-precedence headers/MCP grants/tool caps and violate whole-field precedence. Files/defaults are built into untyped Config first; the finite registry then replaces the exact cache field (with exact env-name origin) before AppConfig deserialization. This still lets valid environment leaves repair malformed lower-file leaves, while arrays/maps replace rather than merge. The earlier receipt wording final builder overrides is superseded by this exact pre-deserialization replacement.","created_at":"2026-08-20T23:02:06.936205405Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:GnnQNPlvNEZp35JadXiNDA+I/8ohf5UCKkSJrMb/gew","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgSjog0F9LUCbKsv62g2BnSf4fH0D7kCW68xbgp+h6bYUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAwO8xQUV/jT/N9g0+ytdFb7wmpZcIqGWIpBc8/9dPexq9NtebHYhdTQuQF8AYZ5nswiP3Ajyt6JKIfrTQeRcuAw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:GnnQNPlvNEZp35JadXiNDA+I/8ohf5UCKkSJrMb/gew","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgSjog0F9LUCbKsv62g2BnSf4fH0D7kCW68xbgp+h6bYUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHkKS5gizn3eKTHrNMxbBIgesRg2YA3qDlTKCJpoyy46H/NaFW2LhscS+BTTiS7YcuwzSCiVKMJtvYkRHwgiNwg="}
